          <thead><tr>
            <th><strong>Origin</strong></th>
            <th><strong>Character</strong></th>
            <th><strong>Colour</strong></th>
            <th><strong>Price / Carat</strong></th>
          </tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Colombia</strong></td>
              <td>The global benchmark</td>
              <td>Rich, warm, vivid green</td>
              <td>₹8,000 – ₹10,00,000+</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Swat / Panjshir</strong></td>
              <td>Bright & lively</td>
              <td>Bright green with visible natural texture</td>
              <td>₹3,000 – ₹3,00,000+</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Zambia</strong></td>
              <td>Strong & durable</td>
              <td>Forest to bluish-green</td>
              <td>₹2,500 – ₹5,00,000+</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Russia</strong></td>
              <td>Cool & structured</td>
              <td>Bluish to grey-green</td>
              <td>₹4,00,000+</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Brazil</strong></td>
              <td>Soft & approachable</td>
              <td>Light to medium green</td>
              <td>₹1,500 – ₹1,50,000+</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody></table>
        <p>Beyond origin, price is shaped by colour vibrancy, saturation, transparency, treatment level, clarity balance, cut quality, and structural stability. With Emerald, a smaller stone with vivid life and natural balance will almost always outperform a larger one that looks flat, dull, or overly treated.</p>
        <p><strong>Ideal weight:</strong> 2–7 carats, depending on the horoscope and Mercury’s strength</p>
        <p><strong>Best metal:</strong> Gold, traditionally. Silver only when astrologically advised.</p>
