    {%- when 'red-coral' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--red_coral">
        <h2>Pricing & Origins</h2>
        <p>Red Coral is an organic gemstone — formed from marine life, not mineral deposits — and its value is shaped by natural colour depth, density, grain quality, and origin. For astrological use, only natural, untreated coral is suitable. Everything else — dyed, reconstructed, resin-filled, or imitation — should be avoided entirely.</p>
        <p><strong>ð®ð¹ Italian Red Coral (Sardinian)</strong> is the global benchmark. Dense, compact, and fine-grained, with a deep vermilion to rich red that is natural and untreated. It is highly suitable for astrological use and remains the most widely trusted source. Price ranges from ₹800 to ₹25,000+ per carat.</p>
        <p><strong>ð¯ðµ Japanese Red Coral (Aka Coral)</strong> is rarer, more refined, and commands a premium. Its colour is even and elegant, its texture smooth and superior in finish. It is a premium astrological choice for those seeking the finest available. Price ranges from ₹4,000 to ₹40,000+ per carat.</p>
        <p>Beyond origin, price is driven by colour uniformity and depth, density and grain tightness, surface finish, and certified natural untreated status. Italian and Japanese origins consistently command premiums — and any claim of Mediterranean origin without independent lab verification should be treated with caution.</p>
        <p><strong>Ideal weight:</strong> Traditionally advised based on the horoscope and Mars's placement. <strong>Best metal:</strong> Gold or Copper traditionally. Silver only when astrologically advised.</p>
      </div>
