    {%- when 'aquamarine' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--aquamarine">
        <p>Pricing & Origins</p>
        <p>Aquamarine's value is shaped by colour tone and depth, transparency, clarity, and cut quality. It is one of the cleaner gemstone categories in terms of treatment — most quality stones are either untreated or gently heat-treated, and the difference is usually clearly disclosed.</p>
        <ul>
        <li>🇷 Brazil is the benchmark — the most trusted and widely respected source for classic Aquamarine. Soft to medium sky-blue, high transparency, and large, clean crystals have made Brazilian material the standard against which others are measured.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Santa Maria (Rare & Premium) is the most coveted expression of Aquamarine — named for the Brazilian mine that first produced it, though the term is now used more broadly for stones of equivalent quality. Deeper ocean-blue, exceptional purity, and genuine rarity place these stones in a separate category of value.</p>
        <ul>
        <li>African Sources (Nigeria, Mozambique, Madagascar) offer fresh light-to-medium blue with clean, contemporary appeal and strong value at equivalent quality levels.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Price ranges from ₹600 to ₹1,50,000+ per carat, depending on colour depth, clarity, size, origin, and whether the stone qualifies as Santa Maria quality. A paler stone with exceptional transparency will often outperform a darker but cloudy one — choose the stone, not just the colour depth.</p>
