        <p>Tiger's Eye is widely accessible. Value is determined by the sharpness of the chatoyant band (the "eye"), colour richness, and polish quality. Fine specimens have a single, centred, sharp eye that moves clearly under light.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'agate' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--agate">
        <p>Agate is generally accessible. Value is determined by pattern quality, colour depth, translucency, and cut. Rare banded varieties or unusual colour formations command higher prices.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'chalcedony' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--chalcedony">
        <p>Chalcedony is widely accessible. Blue chalcedony is most valued, followed by lavender and pink varieties. Value depends on colour evenness, translucency, and surface quality.</p>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="gem-tab"><p>Pricing varies. Contact us for a detailed quote.</p></div>
  {%- endcase -%}